==============================================================================
PART F -- THE PFAFFIAN IS ODD-VALUED (a companion to Redei's hp odd)
==============================================================================
 Observed in PART D: det S(T) for n EVEN is always an ODD perfect square
 (1,9,25,49,81,121 = 1^2,3^2,5^2,7^2,9^2,11^2).  PROOF, one line:
   every off-diagonal entry of S is +-1 = 1 mod 2, so S = J - I mod 2, hence
   Pf(S) = Pf(J-I) = #{perfect matchings of K_n} = (n-1)!! mod 2,
   and (n-1)!! = 1*3*5*...*(n-1) is a product of ODD numbers, so Pf(S) is ODD.
  n=4: Pf values [Fraction(-3, 1), Fraction(-1, 1), Fraction(1, 1), Fraction(3, 1)];  all odd: True;  (n-1)!! = 3 (odd: True)
  n=6: Pf values [Fraction(-9, 1), Fraction(-7, 1), Fraction(-5, 1), Fraction(-3, 1), Fraction(-1, 1), Fraction(1, 1), Fraction(3, 1), Fraction(5, 1)]...;  all odd: True;  (n-1)!! = 15 (odd: True)
  n=8: Pf values [Fraction(-25, 1), Fraction(-23, 1), Fraction(-19, 1), Fraction(-17, 1), Fraction(-15, 1), Fraction(-11, 1), Fraction(-9, 1), Fraction(-7, 1)]...;  all odd: True;  (n-1)!! = 105 (odd: True)
